  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.2.3-rc.2: synthesis-aware IsTransportDead. RtcPeer's IsTransportDead now reads from `_lastObservedPcState` (captured in OnConnectionStateChange handler) BEFORE falling back to the native `_pc.ConnectionState` query. The native query lies on Chromium-under-Playwright: when `BrowserRTCPeerConnection`'s 15s iceDisconnected debounce poller invokes `OnConnectionStateChange(\"failed\")`, the underlying JS native connectionState property stays stuck at `\"connected\"`/`\"disconnected\"` indefinitely. Consulting the synthesised value via the event handler is the only authoritative source. Same Wire.SimplePeer back-reference plumbing as rc.1.",
